'''''Home One''''', also known as '''Headquarters Frigate''', was a modified [[MC80A Home One Type Heavy Star Cruiser|MC80A ''Home One'' Type Heavy Star Cruiser]] of the [[Rebel Alliance Navy|Alliance Fleet]], famous for its role as [[Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]]'s [[flagship]] during the [[Battle of Endor|decisive battle]] fought at [[Endor]].

==Description==
[[File:Home_One_Cross-section.png|thumb|left|250px|A cross-section of ''Home One'']]
''Home One'' was originally constructed as a civilian deep space explorer but was later retrofitted for military service. It featured heavy hull plating and triple-strength shields, along with twenty hangars for bearing other warships and starfighter squadrons.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> It was 1,300 [[meter]]s long, slightly larger than the standard length of an [[MC80 Star Cruiser]]. It was initially armed with [[turbolaser]] cannons, [[ion cannon]]s, and several [[tractor beam]] projectors.<ref name="Databank" /> It was the largest and most advanced ship in the Alliance Fleet.<ref name="UltimateSW" /> The ship's briefing room was originally a [[Hologram|holographic]] [[Holographic amphitheater|amphitheater]].<ref name="RotJ novel">[[Star Wars: Return of the Jedi (paperback novel)|''Star Wars: Return of the Jedi'' junior novelization]]</ref> At least two sections of the ship could detach themselves from the main body, and become fully-independent attack or escape craft should the need arise. The ship's command crew was entirely made up of Mon Calamari. This makeup was due to the fact that the controls were specifically designed for that species. Originally, the ship was built with water-filled passages for the Mon Calamari crew to swim through, but these were later cleared out for other species.<ref name="Complete Vehicles New" />

==History==
===Rebel service===
{{Quote|<s></s>''Home One'', this is Gold Leader.|[[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]], during the Battle of Endor|<ref name="Episode VI" />}}
[[File:Hangar_Bay-AoR.jpg|thumb|left|250px|One of ''Home One''{{'s}} large hangars]]
In [[2 BBY]], ''Home One'' was present during the first official [[Declaration of the Rebel Alliance|gathering]] of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel Alliance]] above the [[planet]] [[Dantooine]].<ref name="Secret Cargo" /> Through its service in the name of overthrowing the [[Galactic Empire]], the ''Home One'' became characterized as a defender of democracy.<ref name="Insider230">{{InsiderCite|230|Launchpad}}</ref>

''Home One'' served as a mobile command center after the Empire discovered and destroyed the main Alliance headquarters on [[Hoth]]. It was also the command ship where [[Mon Mothma]], [[Crix Madine]], [[Admiral]] [[Gial Ackbar]], and a host of other important Alliance officials briefed members of the Rebellion on the upcoming battle on and over [[Endor]]. After Mon Mothma pointed out the strike force's primary objectives and following the departure of [[General]] [[Han Solo]]'s land-based [[Special Forces Trackers Unit|Pathfinder]] commandos, the ship jumped into hyperspace and arrived in the [[Endor system]]<ref name="Episode VI" /> after utilizing the secret hyperspace route known as the [[Sanctuary Pipeline]],<ref name="Moving Target">''[[Moving Target: A Princess Leia Adventure]]''</ref> and immediately entered fierce space-combat during the [[Battle of Endor]]. It served as the lead ship and the command and control center for the attacking Rebel fleet against the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|second Death Star]],<ref name="UltimateSW" /> and was the [[flagship]] of Admiral Ackbar,<ref name="Episode VI" /> earning it the moniker "Headquarters Frigate."<ref name="UltimateSW" />

===New Republic service===
In the [[Standard month|months]] following Endor, the ship would still be undergoing final repairs from the climactic battle, while newly appointed [[Fleet Admiral]] Ackbar would designate the ship as his command vessel, and practice hand-to-hand combat in its holographic chamber to keep his reflexes sharp. In addition, he would order the deployment of members of [[New Republic]] [[New Republic Special Forces|SpecForces]] in a sub-orbital drop onto the planet [[Akiva]] after receiving momentary contact with downed pilot [[Wedge Antilles]] and a brief meeting with New Republic leadership. The members of the operation, unbeknownst to Ackbar, would play an important part in disrupting the [[Imperial Future Council]].<ref name="Aftermath" />

[[File:HomeOne-SWArmada.jpg|thumb|left|250px|''Home One'' precedes the fleet into battle.]]
Later, Admiral Ackbar used ''Home One'' as his command ship during the successful New Republic [[Defense of Kuat|campaign]] to capture the planet [[Kuat]] and the important [[Kuat Drive Yards]]. Ackbar later corresponded with [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]], [[Commodore]] [[Kyrsta Agate]], and [[Chancellor (New Republic)|Chancellor]] Mon Mothma as they received a peace offer from [[Grand Admiral]] [[Rae Sloane]]. ''Home One'' later took part in a brief [[Liberation of Kashyyyk|space battle]] with [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyers]] above [[Kashyyyk]]. The cruiser also accepted the surrender of the Star Destroyer ''[[Neutralizer]]''.<ref name="Life Debt">''[[Aftermath: Life Debt]]''</ref>

''Home One'' would go on to participate in the [[Battle of Jakku]], still under the command of Admiral Ackbar. During the battle, ''Home One'' served as the New Republic fleet's command ship. From ''Home One'', Admiral Ackbar coordinated the battle with other New Republic commanders including Commodore Kyrsta Agate, [[General]] [[Tyben]], and [[Lieutenant General]] [[Brockway]]. ''Home One'' along with Agate's [[Starhawk-class battleship|''Starhawk''-class battleship]] ''[[Concord]]'' took part in the assault on the Imperial Star Destroyers enveloping the Imperial [[Super Star Destroyer]] ''[[Ravager]]'', which served as the Imperial command ship. From the bridge of ''Home One'', Ackbar watched as the ''Concord'' used its powerful [[tractor beam projector]] to drag the ''Ravager'' to [[Jakku]]'s surface. This turned the tide of the battle decisively in the New Republic's favor, leading to the Empire's capitulation and the [[Galactic Concordance]], which ended the [[Galactic Civil War]].<ref name="Empire's End">''[[Aftermath: Empire's End]]''</ref>

Following the war's conclusion, ''Home One'' continued to serve the New Republic, accompanied by an escort of X-wings.<ref name="Part One" /> Around [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Ahsoka series date" /> former [[Jedi Knight]] [[Ahsoka Tano]] met up with New Republic general [[Hera Syndulla]] to discuss the missing [[prisoner]] [[Morgan Elsbeth]] on the cruiser. Mon Calamari, too, were still serving on the ship, with one such officer asking Syndulla for an update on the situation on behalf of the [[Senate Defense Council]].<ref name="Part One" /> Sometime later, ''Home One'' was accompanied by a [[Hera Syndulla's fleet|massive fleet]] of [[EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate]]s, [[CR90 corvette]]s, [[Sphyrna-class Hammerhead corvette|''Sphyrna''-class Hammerhead corvettes]], [[Defender-class cruiser|''Defender''-class cruisers]], and a squadron of A-Wings. General Syndulla called a meeting with [[Chancellor (New Republic)|Chancellor]] [[Mon Mothma]] and members of the [[New Republic Senate]], including [[Senator]] [[Hamato Xiono]], to discuss the threat of [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]]'s return and sent New Republic forces on [[Seatos]] to stop it. Despite Chancellor Mothma's support, the other senators refused to believe that Thrawn is still alive and denied Syndulla's request.<ref name="Part Three" />

===Resistance service===
''Home One'' later belonged to the [[Resistance]] under General Leia Organa. [[Commander]] [[Poe Dameron]] was assigned his [[Operation: Sabre Strike|first big mission]] on ''Home One''.<ref name="BTA" />

==Behind the scenes==
''Home One'' first appeared as the Rebel Alliance's command ship in [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'' Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="Episode VI" />

